			"Message": "chore(air): Add generated gRPC client and server code\n\nThis commit introduces the auto-generated Rust code from the air.proto file using prost-build. The generated code includes all message structs and the gRPC client and server implementations for the AirService, enabling remote service interactions for authentication, updates, downloads, indexing, status monitoring, resource management, and configuration handling.",
			"SHA": "5a8bfb05c44194fe59a41c4241cfd0e51adbd895"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-01-28T08:15:45Z",
			"File": [
				"⠁⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				32,
				1
			],
			"Message": "chore(air): Standardize dependencies to use workspace versions\n\nThis commit refactors the dependency management in Cargo.toml to leverage workspace-wide version specifications. By moving from hardcoded version numbers to `workspace = true` references, we ensure consistent dependency versions across the entire Land workspace, reducing the risk of version conflicts and simplifying future updates.\n\nKey changes implemented:\n- Updated core dependencies (tokio, tonic, serde, etc.) to use workspace versions for unified management\n- Added futures-util dependency to complement the existing futures crate with additional utilities\n- Removed tokio-stream and IPC-related dependencies (tokio-serial, tokio-pipe) as they are no longer required for the current Air daemon implementation\n- Retained specific versions for walkdir, ring, and sysinfo where workspace configuration isn't applicable or necessary\n\nThis alignment with Rust workspace best practices improves maintainability and ensures all crates in the ecosystem use synchronized dependency versions.",
			"SHA": "14e2c0498205bd039a44242656a583e4aa628de3"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-01-28T08:11:40Z",
			"File": [
				"⡏⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				32,
				4
			],
			"Message": "feat(air): Add core background services for downloader, indexing, and updates\n\nThis commit introduces three essential background services that form the operational backbone of the Air daemon, providing critical functionality for the Land ecosystem.\n\nThe Downloader service handles resilient background downloading of files, extensions, and dependencies with comprehensive features:\n- Retry logic with exponential backoff for network failures\n- Progress tracking and status monitoring\n- Checksum verification for downloaded content\n- Background cache cleanup and download management\n- Support for both direct downloads and cached operations\n\nThe Indexing service provides advanced file search and metadata extraction capabilities:\n- Directory indexing with configurable file patterns and size limits\n- Content-based search with line-level matching\n- MIME type detection and programming language identification\n- File metadata extraction including checksums and line counts\n- Background periodic re-indexing of common directories\n\nThe Updates service manages the complete update lifecycle for the Land ecosystem:\n- Automated update checking with configurable intervals\n- Secure download and verification of update packages\n- Version comparison and update availability tracking\n- Background update checks and auto-download capabilities\n- Comprehensive update status monitoring\n\nAdditionally, this commit includes a minor build configuration fix correcting a typo in the Cargo.toml binary target name from 'ame' to 'name'.\n\nThese services integrate with the existing gRPC infrastructure and application state management, providing the foundation for remote service operations including file management, search capabilities, and system updates.",
			"SHA": "173e658073afef669dbc62a3a8f4c299e3482f7f"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-01-28T07:54:28Z",
			"File": [
				"⣿⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				26,
				5
			],
			"Message": "feat(air): Add gRPC service skeleton with authentication\n\nThis commit introduces the foundational components for the Air daemon service, which provides background operations for Land. The changes establish a complete gRPC service definition and initial implementation, focusing on authentication as the first operational capability.\n\nKey additions:\n- Proto/air.proto: Defines the AirService gRPC interface with comprehensive RPC methods for authentication, update checks, file downloads, indexing, status monitoring, resource management, and configuration handling.\n- Source/Authentication/mod.rs: Implements a full authentication service with user credential validation, session token generation, encrypted password storage, and background session cleanup tasks.\n- Source/Vine/Error.rs: Provides specialized error types for gRPC client operations, including transport, serialization, and authentication errors.\n- Source/Vine/Generated/mod.rs: Serves as a placeholder module for the auto-generated gRPC code from the proto definitions.\n- build.rs: Adds a build script that compiles the air.proto file and generates the corresponding gRPC client and server code during the build process.\n\nThis infrastructure enables remote service interactions through a well-defined protocol, supporting future extensions for update management, file operations, and system monitoring. The authentication service includes secure credential handling with cryptographic key generation and session management, forming the core security layer for the daemon.",
			"SHA": "175292053cab016c0fb4729b7cc17f5955e5580b"
		}
	],
